Z||000028||KnightRyder31||05-29-2001||04:36 PM||||I like the Doors.<BR>I also like a lot of other Classic Rock bands. And I like some modern rock also.<BR>I HATE RAP!!!!!!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000029||KnightRyder31||05-29-2001||04:38 PM||||BTW, I LOVE SATCH!!!!!<BR>War is a great song.<BR>In my opinion Satch is the greatest guitarist to live!||||reg||1
Z||000030||Taijiguy||05-29-2001||04:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KnightRyder31<BR><B>BTW, I LOVE SATCH!!!!!<BR>War is a great song.<BR>In my opinion Satch is the greatest guitarist to live!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>For simple blinding speed and technical prowess, he definitely get's one of my votes. If you want to hear some stuff that just oozes emotion and has the kind of sound that speaks right to your soul, check out some old Leslie West (Mountain) Nantucket Sleighride, For Yasgurs Farm, songs like that. Absolutely beautiful guitar work. Also, check out some old Robin Trower. Bridge of Sighs, Day of the Eagle, tunes like those. It's close call to me which has the best guitar sound. Both are great.||||reg||1
Z||000031||Songman||05-29-2001||06:15 PM||||Hate to burst the bubble of people who like to talk about '3 chord songs' but most songs are 3 chords. That is just fact of music. Sure, you can throw in some variations but most songs are still 3 chord arrangements. A lot of the biggest songs in history only had two chords... I am pretty sure I have heard some of those metal banging songs that only had one - played REAL loud!<P>And before anyone says "Well, that is because you are country".. I played in a rock and roll band for about 6 years before I started playing country. It is all the same.<P>And I still love a lot of rock n roll music. Mostly the 70s stuff, but I do like some new stuff. Someone mentioned Creed.. great group! Probably one of my favorites since U2 went commercial..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
